Trust me, I just listed a quick few things that I find very wrong about the numbers on that spreadsheet. I could list a lot more (Advanced Chairman is easier than normal if going by those numbers and you want me to trust that sheet? Not a chance). Picking out things that dont make sense in a bank of data is a fine practice because it calls into question how reliable that data actually is.It&#39;s fine for a rough guide, but I wouldn&#39;t put much stock into it as far as using it to back up an argument.&nbsp;

[/quote]
True, but the # of heroes scores should be more accurate than average, because they have the largest sample size and are probably less subject to experienced player biases.
